<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Pilot study principles">
  <div><strong>Feasibility first</strong><span>Can the future study be done well, and should it proceed?</span></div>
  <div><strong>Use progression criteria</strong><span>Recruitment, completion, data quality, adherence and tolerance should guide the next step.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Keep status explicit</strong><span>Concept, planned, approved, recruiting, completed and analyzed are different stages.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Current public pilot portfolio</p>
  <h2>Questions in methods and feasibility development</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Pilot concept</th><th>Status</th><th>Main question</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Multi-measure hydration assessment</strong></td><td>Protocol development / planned</td><td>Can complementary hydration measures be collected reliably without over-relying on one spot value?</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Preparation and tolerability workflow</strong></td><td>Methods development</td><td>Can preparation, timing, intake, adherence and gastrointestinal tolerance be recorded consistently?</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Clinical observation framework</strong></td><td>Exploratory design</td><td>Which routine observations could help define later clinical questions?</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What pilots are for</p>
    <h2>Answer design questions before efficacy questions</h2>
    <p>Useful pilot outputs include recruitment, retention, sample completeness, adherence, acceptability, protocol deviations and whether planned outcomes can be measured consistently.</p>
    <p>A small apparent difference can be interesting, but a pilot that is not designed or powered for efficacy should not be marketed as proof of effectiveness.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Progression criteria</p>
  <h2>Decide in advance what would make a pilot advance, change or stop</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Recruitment</h3><p>Can the intended population be identified and enrolled at a workable rate?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Protocol completion</h3><p>Can participants and staff follow preparation, timing, sampling and follow-up?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Data quality</h3><p>Are measurements complete and consistent enough for the planned analysis?</p></article>
    <article><h3>Safety & tolerance</h3><p>Are symptoms, adverse events and stopping reasons captured clearly?</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Research governance</p>
    <h2>“Pilot” is not an exemption</h2>
    <p>Ethics and regulatory requirements depend on the actual study activities, including intervention assignment, sampling and product conditions of use.</p>
    <p>Public descriptions should follow the finalized protocol classification, not try to define it through marketing language.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Current status</span>
    <h3>Questions are public before answers exist.</h3>
    <p>No clinical or product-effect result is implied unless a later update explicitly reports verified study status and findings.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

